1
00:00:27,600 --> 00:00:29,359
On your marks

2
00:00:42,719 --> 00:00:44,000
Get set

3
00:01:03,600 --> 00:01:04,400
Chen Hao

4
00:01:08,400 --> 00:01:09,560
It's really you.

5
00:01:10,519 --> 00:01:12,319
Wait, what are you doing here?

6
00:01:12,719 --> 00:01:13,799
You know why.

7
00:01:14,120 --> 00:01:14,840
How would I kno-

8
00:01:14,840 --> 00:01:16,000
I... I don't know.

9
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:16,640
I don't even know myself.

10
00:01:16,640 --> 00:01:17,719
Stop playing dumb.

11
00:01:19,879 --> 00:01:20,879
That race...

12
00:01:22,280 --> 00:01:23,480
What the hell did you do?

13
00:02:01,760 --> 00:02:03,079
You did it on purpose that day.

14
00:02:03,359 --> 00:02:04,319
You're overthinking it.

15
00:02:04,599 --> 00:02:05,680
Xie Xin, you might fool others,

16
00:02:05,680 --> 00:02:06,680
but you can't fool me.

17
00:02:06,680 --> 00:02:10,080
Fool you? Why would I? I'm not lying!

18
00:02:16,599 --> 00:02:17,479
That guy

19
00:02:18,599 --> 00:02:19,599
approached me too.

20
00:02:27,080 --> 00:02:28,919
If I don't say anything, and you don't,

21
00:02:29,719 --> 00:02:31,080
no one will ever know.

22
00:02:31,159 --> 00:02:32,319
But Boss Wang...

23
00:02:32,599 --> 00:02:34,319
What do you compete for?

24
00:02:34,759 --> 00:02:35,719
To win, obviously.

25
00:02:36,280 --> 00:02:37,400
And after you win?

26
00:02:40,199 --> 00:02:42,520
After winning, you get attention.

27
00:02:42,520 --> 00:02:43,919
Then you get brand endorsements.

28
00:02:44,520 --> 00:02:45,879
And then you get money.

29
00:02:47,439 --> 00:02:48,759
But can you guarantee that

30
00:02:48,759 --> 00:02:50,400
you'll keep winning until then?

31
00:02:54,439 --> 00:02:56,520
You know how this industry is.

32
00:02:56,719 --> 00:02:57,919
Any single loss

33
00:02:58,400 --> 00:03:00,439
could ruin you forever.

34
00:03:07,280 --> 00:03:07,800
Boss Wang,

35
00:03:07,800 --> 00:03:08,360
Today,

36
00:03:08,360 --> 00:03:10,319
I'm really not here to discuss winning or losing.

37
00:03:10,439 --> 00:03:12,599
I'm here to discuss a new way to make money.

38
00:03:13,000 --> 00:03:14,919
This kind of easy money

39
00:03:15,840 --> 00:03:16,919
won't always be around.

40
00:03:22,520 --> 00:03:24,199
No, why would I drop the baton on purpose?

41
00:03:24,199 --> 00:03:26,439
Chen Hao, we've known each other since middle school.

42
00:03:26,680 --> 00:03:27,919
Then we got into college together.

43
00:03:27,919 --> 00:03:29,479
We've always practiced running together.

44
00:03:29,479 --> 00:03:31,479
I've always been the most competitive one!

45
00:03:31,520 --> 00:03:32,560
I really care about winning.

46
00:03:32,560 --> 00:03:33,479
Don't you know that?

47
00:03:34,360 --> 00:03:36,240
Besides, in competitive sports,

48
00:03:36,240 --> 00:03:37,680
it's very... easy to make mistakes.

49
00:03:37,680 --> 00:03:39,120
You make mistakes if you're too nervous,

50
00:03:39,120 --> 00:03:40,120
and you make mistakes if you're too relaxed.

51
00:03:40,120 --> 00:03:41,159
Get back to your corner.

52
00:03:43,120 --> 00:03:44,560
The match begins!

53
00:03:45,719 --> 00:03:46,520
No, no, no!

54
00:03:46,520 --> 00:03:47,280
That's not what I meant.

55
00:03:47,280 --> 00:03:49,199
We don't need to fight! No need to fight!

56
00:03:49,560 --> 00:03:51,319
Let me just explain this clearly.

57
00:03:52,240 --> 00:03:53,560
I'm telling the truth, Chen Hao!

58
00:03:53,560 --> 00:03:55,280
Tell the truth!

59
00:04:03,280 --> 00:04:05,919
Chen Hao, have you been secretly practicing boxing? I...

60
00:04:06,080 --> 00:04:07,719
You're crazy! I told you the truth!

61
00:04:07,719 --> 00:04:08,800
Listen to me!

62
00:04:09,120 --> 00:04:10,280
Ref! Referee!

63
00:04:10,280 --> 00:04:10,840
Time out! Time out!

64
00:04:10,840 --> 00:04:12,039
I can't see out of my left eye!

65
00:04:12,039 --> 00:04:13,159
I'm telling you, I can't fight anymore!

66
00:04:13,520 --> 00:04:14,639
Why did you make that mistake?

67
00:04:16,079 --> 00:04:18,560
Why would there be a reason for a mistake!

68
00:04:18,680 --> 00:04:19,079
I...

69
00:04:19,079 --> 00:04:20,000
Still making excuses!

70
00:04:20,720 --> 00:04:21,399
Wait! Wait!

71
00:04:21,399 --> 00:04:22,399
Chen Hao! Chen Hao!

72
00:04:23,160 --> 00:04:24,120
I'll tell you the truth.

73
00:04:24,399 --> 00:04:25,519
I didn't want to do match-fixing!

74
00:04:25,519 --> 00:04:26,519
I ran as hard as I could!

75
00:04:26,519 --> 00:04:27,720
But because I was so afraid of making a mistake,

76
00:04:27,720 --> 00:04:28,560
that's exactly why I made one!

77
00:04:28,560 --> 00:04:29,720
Do you understand?

78
00:04:29,759 --> 00:04:31,199
So did you take the money or not?

79
00:04:31,600 --> 00:04:32,399
I didn't!

80
00:04:33,000 --> 00:04:33,920
Bullshit!

81
00:04:34,240 --> 00:04:35,040
Boss Wang,

82
00:04:35,519 --> 00:04:36,519
why are you here?

83
00:04:36,720 --> 00:04:39,519
Don't disappoint me this time either.

84
00:04:40,399 --> 00:04:41,680
What do you mean "either"?

85
00:04:56,920 --> 00:04:57,720
What's this?

86
00:04:59,279 --> 00:05:00,720
Sorry for the trouble.

87
00:05:03,040 --> 00:05:04,399
No, it's not like that.

88
00:05:05,120 --> 00:05:05,839
Thanks for your hard work.

89
00:05:06,199 --> 00:05:07,120
Who? No.

90
00:05:07,199 --> 00:05:08,600
It really wasn't like that.

91
00:05:08,879 --> 00:05:09,800
As agreed.

92
00:05:10,759 --> 00:05:13,240
100,000. The password is your birthday.

93
00:05:13,759 --> 00:05:15,319
Who agreed to anything with you?

94
00:05:15,319 --> 00:05:17,279
Yes, we... we lost the race.

95
00:05:17,319 --> 00:05:19,199
But that was because I was too nervous.

96
00:05:19,199 --> 00:05:20,600
There was a mistake with the baton handoff.

97
00:05:20,680 --> 00:05:22,040
So I let my teammates down,

98
00:05:22,040 --> 00:05:22,759
which caused us to lose.

99
00:05:22,759 --> 00:05:23,720
What does this have to do with...

100
00:05:28,360 --> 00:05:29,360
A pleasure working with you.

101
00:05:31,920 --> 00:05:33,680
No! Who's working with you?

102
00:05:34,920 --> 00:05:35,920
Hold on a second.

103
00:05:37,279 --> 00:05:38,920
I didn't do match-fixing!

104
00:05:38,920 --> 00:05:39,959
I didn't!

105
00:05:39,959 --> 00:05:41,199
It doesn't matter.

106
00:05:41,800 --> 00:05:43,680
We only care about the result.

107
00:05:43,759 --> 00:05:45,360
Why? Says who?

108
00:05:45,360 --> 00:05:46,600
All I had was the process!

109
00:05:46,600 --> 00:05:47,920
I didn't do match-fixing!

110
00:05:48,000 --> 00:05:49,319
I didn't do match-fixing!

111
00:05:49,319 --> 00:05:50,199
I didn't do match-fixing!

112
00:05:50,199 --> 00:05:51,480
It was just a mistake!

113
00:05:53,600 --> 00:05:54,160
Okay, Boss Wang.

114
00:05:54,160 --> 00:05:55,759
Tell me, did you bet on me losing or...

115
00:05:58,199 --> 00:05:59,480
Anyway, that's the situation.

116
00:05:59,680 --> 00:06:00,800
I took the money.

117
00:06:04,560 --> 00:06:05,360
That money...

118
00:06:06,240 --> 00:06:07,639
I wanted to split it among the four of us.

119
00:06:08,600 --> 00:06:10,240
But splitting it would mean admitting to it.

120
00:06:10,240 --> 00:06:11,639
I couldn't admit to it, you know?

121
00:06:17,120 --> 00:06:17,879
Do you understand?

122
00:06:17,879 --> 00:06:20,759
I understand. I get it, I get it.

123
00:06:21,639 --> 00:06:24,519
Do you think we care about your filthy money?

124
00:07:16,240 --> 00:07:17,000
Neck and neck.

125
00:07:17,800 --> 00:07:19,399
You couldn't tell I slowed down early?

126
00:07:19,399 --> 00:07:20,319
Bullshit.

127
00:07:22,360 --> 00:07:23,000
By the way, Xie Xin.

128
00:07:23,480 --> 00:07:25,399
Tell me, if we keep running like this,

129
00:07:25,519 --> 00:07:26,560
will we get anywhere?

130
00:07:27,519 --> 00:07:28,199
I don't know.

131
00:07:28,519 --> 00:07:29,279
What do you think?

132
00:07:29,279 --> 00:07:31,079
I... I don't know either.

133
00:07:33,160 --> 00:07:35,120
By the way, promise me something.

134
00:07:35,560 --> 00:07:36,120
Shoot.

135
00:07:36,959 --> 00:07:38,079
If there ever comes a day

136
00:07:38,639 --> 00:07:39,920
when we become opponents,

137
00:07:40,680 --> 00:07:43,000
make sure you go all out.

138
00:07:44,199 --> 00:07:44,800
Chen Hao!

139
00:07:45,399 --> 00:07:46,120
What?

140
00:07:46,120 --> 00:07:47,000
Neck and neck!

141
00:07:48,000 --> 00:07:49,000
You played me!

142
00:07:50,920 --> 00:07:51,560
Stop right there!

143
00:07:55,079 --> 00:07:55,720
Tell me.

144
00:07:56,519 --> 00:07:59,560
Where did you spend all that money?

145
00:08:01,319 --> 00:08:02,920
Your mom was sick back then, wasn't she?

146
00:08:04,120 --> 00:08:05,399
And medical treatments cost money.

147
00:08:06,600 --> 00:08:07,360
So?

148
00:08:08,480 --> 00:08:09,519
What are you trying to say?

149
00:08:10,560 --> 00:08:12,040
I spent it on her medical bills.

150
00:08:34,000 --> 00:08:35,039
Don't think

151
00:08:36,360 --> 00:08:37,799
that I'll thank you for doing this.

152
00:08:39,679 --> 00:08:40,279
There's no need.

153
00:08:41,200 --> 00:08:43,320
I only gave you the money to make amends.

154
00:08:47,080 --> 00:08:47,559
But you...

155
00:08:49,039 --> 00:08:50,320
But you still broke

156
00:08:51,200 --> 00:08:52,840
our agreement, didn't you?

157
00:08:55,080 --> 00:08:57,240
The score is now 19 to 19.

158
00:08:57,399 --> 00:08:58,320
Tied.

159
00:09:00,039 --> 00:09:00,720
Come on.

160
00:09:02,039 --> 00:09:03,320
Go all out. Come on, get up.

161
00:09:05,919 --> 00:09:06,840
Go all out.

162
00:09:50,759 --> 00:09:51,720
The match is over.

163
00:09:52,840 --> 00:09:53,960
The winner is Chen Hao.

164
00:09:54,879 --> 00:09:56,399
Challenger, please exit.

165
00:09:57,200 --> 00:09:58,559
Shock him.

166
00:10:01,120 --> 00:10:03,399
Xie Xin, you tricked me.

167
00:10:03,799 --> 00:10:05,279
I want a rematch with you.

168
00:10:05,519 --> 00:10:06,720
Get up, Xie Xin.

169
00:10:07,919 --> 00:10:08,960
Xie Xin.

170
00:10:09,279 --> 00:10:11,159
Let's go. Let's go.

171
00:10:12,519 --> 00:10:14,000
No wonder you're so easy to fool.

172
00:10:20,639 --> 00:10:21,879
I think I've figured it out.

173
00:10:22,399 --> 00:10:23,440
This whole setup of yours...

174
00:10:25,080 --> 00:10:25,799
Where is everyone?

175
00:10:26,559 --> 00:10:29,399
A reality show. The Truman Show.

176
00:10:30,440 --> 00:10:33,000
Ex... Ex... Exchange, right?

177
00:10:33,519 --> 00:10:35,399
Very mediocre. Really mediocre.

178
00:10:35,399 --> 00:10:37,360
This piece of junk won't kill me.

179
00:10:37,639 --> 00:10:39,120
I'll give you credit for one thing.

180
00:10:40,120 --> 00:10:41,320
You're really good at digging.

181
00:10:41,320 --> 00:10:42,399
You really did your homework on me.

182
00:10:42,399 --> 00:10:44,559
Digging up my dark past, right?

183
00:10:45,080 --> 00:10:47,559
Bringing in old man Lin, Chen Hao...

184
00:10:47,559 --> 00:10:48,759
I can't even reach these people.

185
00:10:48,759 --> 00:10:49,960
How did you manage to contact them?

186
00:10:52,480 --> 00:10:53,759
But let me just say something.

187
00:10:55,279 --> 00:10:57,240
You're not getting any drama out of me.

188
00:10:58,960 --> 00:11:00,279
No apologies.

189
00:11:00,720 --> 00:11:02,360
No remorse.

190
00:11:02,639 --> 00:11:04,000
No revenge.

191
00:11:04,000 --> 00:11:05,240
No reconciliation.

192
00:11:05,240 --> 00:11:06,519
You're getting absolutely nothing.

193
00:11:06,639 --> 00:11:08,440
Because I'm not a bad guy.

194
00:11:08,440 --> 00:11:09,960
And we aren't enemies.

195
00:11:10,000 --> 00:11:11,159
There's no reason to apologize.

196
00:11:11,360 --> 00:11:12,440
Everything I've done...

197
00:11:12,440 --> 00:11:13,759
I can clearly explain.

198
00:11:13,759 --> 00:11:14,720
I have my logic.

199
00:11:14,759 --> 00:11:15,720
I have my reasons.

200
00:11:17,360 --> 00:11:18,440
Do you hear me?

201
00:11:20,399 --> 00:11:22,639
Who in this world doesn't owe someone a little something?

202
00:12:00,279 --> 00:12:01,360
Are you okay?

203
00:12:07,600 --> 00:12:09,360
Why are you here?

204
00:12:11,519 --> 00:12:13,080
Am I not supposed to be here?

205
00:12:20,360 --> 00:12:22,919
Thank you for setting all this up today, Honey.

206
00:12:23,559 --> 00:12:24,360
I really love it.

207
00:12:24,759 --> 00:12:25,720
You're welcome, Honey.

208
00:12:26,519 --> 00:12:28,399
And thanks to you and him

209
00:12:28,720 --> 00:12:29,759
for coming here.

210
00:12:30,679 --> 00:12:31,559
Did you hear that?

211
00:12:32,120 --> 00:12:33,440
Daddy says thank you to us.

212
00:12:34,440 --> 00:12:35,240
Cheers.

213
00:12:36,039 --> 00:12:37,240
Happy anniversary, Honey.

214
00:12:37,519 --> 00:12:38,320
Happy anniversary.

215
00:12:48,840 --> 00:12:51,120
What's wrong? Why are you looking at me like that?

216
00:12:53,879 --> 00:12:54,519
Handsome.

217
00:12:54,879 --> 00:12:55,679
Handsome.

218
00:12:57,960 --> 00:12:59,039
Is there any compliment...

219
00:13:00,679 --> 00:13:02,639
...about my inner qualities?

220
00:13:03,840 --> 00:13:04,639
Kind.

221
00:13:05,399 --> 00:13:06,039
Kind.

222
00:13:06,559 --> 00:13:07,759
That doesn't sound cool.

223
00:13:08,759 --> 00:13:10,000
Eloquent.

224
00:13:10,320 --> 00:13:11,720
Deceptive.

225
00:13:13,480 --> 00:13:14,360
A smooth talker.

226
00:13:14,360 --> 00:13:16,000
A... a smooth talker.

227
00:13:17,279 --> 00:13:18,240
W-What's wrong?

228
00:13:18,480 --> 00:13:19,159
Nothing.

229
00:13:19,799 --> 00:13:20,639
A smooth talker.

230
00:13:20,840 --> 00:13:22,159
A very... very smooth talker.

231
00:13:24,559 --> 00:13:25,240
Alright.

232
00:13:26,039 --> 00:13:27,120
Here, this is for you.

233
00:13:30,799 --> 00:13:31,799
Thanks for the compliment.

234
00:13:35,039 --> 00:13:36,360
That was very... very thoughtful.

235
00:13:53,279 --> 00:13:54,559
Happy anniversary, Honey.

236
00:13:56,159 --> 00:13:57,000
Thank you, Honey.

237
00:13:57,000 --> 00:13:57,919
You're welcome, Honey.

238
00:14:04,679 --> 00:14:05,320
What's wrong?

239
00:14:05,519 --> 00:14:06,840
Wait, your finger might be a little swollen.

240
00:14:08,039 --> 00:14:09,600
I bought it too small. You wear mine.

241
00:14:10,039 --> 00:14:11,320
Wear mine. Wear mine.

242
00:14:11,679 --> 00:14:13,120
Right, I'll wear yours. Let's swap.

243
00:14:13,120 --> 00:14:13,720
Here, put it on.

244
00:14:13,720 --> 00:14:14,440
This works, right?

245
00:14:14,440 --> 00:14:15,240
Just wear it like this for now.

246
00:14:15,679 --> 00:14:16,600
You can't wear it on your pinky.

247
00:14:16,600 --> 00:14:17,000
Why not?

248
00:14:17,000 --> 00:14:17,840
The pinky means divorce.

249
00:14:20,320 --> 00:14:21,799
Give it to me, give it to me.

250
00:14:22,039 --> 00:14:23,000
It's fine. It's fine.

251
00:14:26,159 --> 00:14:26,799
It looks good.

252
00:14:27,120 --> 00:14:27,799
It suits you.

253
00:14:27,919 --> 00:14:28,600
Thank you, Honey.

254
00:14:31,679 --> 00:14:32,480
I love it.

255
00:14:35,639 --> 00:14:36,360
What's wrong?

256
00:14:37,440 --> 00:14:39,320
My stomach hurts a little.

257
00:14:39,840 --> 00:14:41,360
Then... then let's go to the hospital.

258
00:14:42,000 --> 00:14:42,639
It's fine, it's fine.

259
00:14:42,639 --> 00:14:43,360
It'll pass in a minute.

260
00:14:43,360 --> 00:14:44,240
We already ordered the food.

261
00:14:44,360 --> 00:14:46,360
Honey, let's go to the hospital to get checked,

262
00:14:46,360 --> 00:14:48,200
then we can eat in peace, okay?

263
00:14:49,279 --> 00:14:50,000
Okay.

264
00:15:06,000 --> 00:15:07,279
Let me, Honey. Give me the bag.

265
00:15:07,799 --> 00:15:08,440
How are you feeling?

266
00:15:08,559 --> 00:15:09,360
I don't feel well.

267
00:15:09,440 --> 00:15:10,240
Still not feeling well, right?

268
00:15:10,240 --> 00:15:10,840
Yeah.

269
00:15:11,120 --> 00:15:12,559
Okay, let's go to the hospital right now.

270
00:15:12,559 --> 00:15:13,440
We'll get you checked up right away.

271
00:15:13,440 --> 00:15:14,360
No, no.

272
00:15:14,360 --> 00:15:15,720
You've been drinking. You need a designated driver service.

273
00:15:15,759 --> 00:15:16,840
Just one sip. Just one sip.

274
00:15:16,840 --> 00:15:18,080
I'm fine. Just trust me, okay?

275
00:15:18,080 --> 00:15:18,759
No, no way.

276
00:15:18,759 --> 00:15:19,799
Trust me. Let's get to the hospital first.

277
00:15:19,799 --> 00:15:20,799
Okay, come on, come on.

278
00:15:20,840 --> 00:15:22,639
It's safer if you get a designated driver service.

279
00:15:22,639 --> 00:15:24,240
Listen to me, the hospital... it's not far.

280
00:15:24,240 --> 00:15:25,080
No.

281
00:15:25,240 --> 00:15:26,120
What's wrong? What's wrong?

282
00:15:26,399 --> 00:15:27,399
I need to sit down for a minute.

283
00:15:27,399 --> 00:15:28,120
Here, come here.

284
00:15:28,120 --> 00:15:29,320
Get in the car, get in, get in.

285
00:15:29,600 --> 00:15:31,519
